# Windows' core.autocrlf=true only skips line-ending conversion on files it can
# tell are binary. Its heuristic (look for a NUL byte in the first ~8000 bytes)
# can miss compressed formats like APKs, which is how public/apps/CFD.apk and
# Seller.apk ended up as corrupted zip archives in git history — no NUL byte
# early enough in those two files, so autocrlf mangled bytes on commit.
*.apk binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
